body:
### Tested versions

v4.7.beta4.mono.official [dff2b9bb6]


### System information

Windows 11 - Godot 4.7 beta 4, Vulkan (Forward+) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 3060

### Issue description

Overriding _Process in C# has a really high overhead, so much that it is significantly better to store a Collection of the nodes in the scene and manually calling them in a main _Process function. Which is clearly not intended.

### Steps to reproduce

Create an empty godot project with an empty main scene.
Create another scene containing only
```c#
public partial class NodeTest : Node2D
{
    public bool active = false;
    public override void _Process(double delta)
    {
        function(delta);
    }

    public void function(double delta)
    {
        if(active)
            Visible = !Visible;
    }
}
```
And in the main scene add one
```c#
public partial class Tracker : Node
{
    public static PackedScene packedNode = GD.Load<PackedScene>("res://node_test.tscn");

    public Collection<NodeTest> nodeTests = [];

    public override void _Ready()
    {
        base._Ready();
        for(int i = 0;i != 50000;++i)
        {
            NodeTest node = packedNode.Instantiate() as NodeTest;
            AddChild(node);
            nodeTests.Add(node);
        }
    }

    public override void _Process(double delta)
    {
        base._Process(delta);
        foreach(NodeTest nodeTest in nodeTests)
            nodeTest.function(delta);
    }
}
```

And then start up godot with either NodeTest._Process commented out or Tracker._Process commented out.
Both are functionally identical, but using NodeTest._Process leads to really low performance.

Performance with NodeTest._Process
<img width="495" height="668" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/076becea-6630-4797-8bde-aff66abc7b1c" />
Performance with a Collection
<img width="511" height="663" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7328a60d-d4dc-4d2b-acc7-e8e6b0bc6424" />


It is expected to have _Process taking a little longer, but that is 30ms for 50k boolean checks, order of magnitudes above simply keeping track of nodes and calling a Process function yourself.



